tware products and software-enabled services to financial services and healthcare industries in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia Pacific. The company owns and operates technology stack across securities accounting; front-office functions, such as trading and modeling; middle-office functions comprising portfolio management and reporting; back-office functions, such as accounting, performance measurement, reconciliation, reporting, processing and clearing, and compliance and tax reporting; and healthcare solutions consisting of claims adjudication, benefit management, care management, and business intelligence solutions. It also offers software-enabled services, such as SS&C GlobeOp, Global Investor and Distribution Solutions, SS&C Retirement Solutions, Calastone, Managed Services, Data Solutions, ALPS Advisors, and Virtual Data Rooms, as well as pharmacy, healthcare administration, and health outcomes optimization solutions. In addition, the company provides portfolio management, operations, and accounting software; trading software; intelligent automation solutions; banking and lending solutions, as well as research, analytics, risk, and training solutions. The company also provides professional services that includes consulting and implementation services consisting of initial system installation, conversion of historical data, and ongoing training and support, as well as product support services. SS&C Technologies Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Windsor, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William C. Stone | Founder, Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $9.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $218K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $58K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 43\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["SS&C Technologies Holdings, Inc is a large-cap technology business with a $18.5B market cap on $6.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 47%.","The business throws off $1.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (48% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{